From 754e6b69d152d52f4b7b67119cbf4baf5564ab9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: D-Ogi <6542335+D-Ogi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:40:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] radv: admit a bounded GENERAL queue count for bound
 hosted queues

The native D3D12 engine (ABI 1.1 draft, V7) takes one GENERAL VkQueue
for its internal queue and one for every application queue, and hosted
RADV reports a single GENERAL queue. Two application queues plus the
internal one need at least three.

Add struct bc250_host_queue_binding, a private structure chained to
VkInstanceCreateInfo next to struct bc250_host. It opts the instance
into runtime-bound queues and carries the function table that a later
change fills. It is validated as strictly as struct bc250_host and
refused without one.

With the opt-in, and a winsys that can create bindable contexts, the
GENERAL family reports RADV_BC250_BOUND_GENERAL_QUEUES (8): the
internal queue and seven application queues. vkCreateDevice refuses
more GENERAL queues than that. No winsys provides ctx_create_bindable
yet, so the count stays 1 until each queue owns its context; no two
VkQueues ever share a context.

Instances without the structure, the D3D11 bridge among them, are
unchanged. The binding contract is a draft pending T0.
